   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Comparative Study of Speech-to-Text Models for Noisy Real-World Audio\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides an interactive benchmark analysis and demonstration of three Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) systems:\n",
    "1. **Faster-Whisper (`base`, CTranslate2 INT8)**\n",
    "2. **OpenAI Whisper (`base`, PyTorch FP32)**\n",
    "3. **Wav2Vec 2.0 (`facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h`, CTC)**\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluated under both **clean** and **controlled noisy conditions (10 dB SNR)** on a fixed evaluation subset of speech audio."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install dependencies (for Google Colab execution)\n",
    "!pip install -q faster-whisper openai-whisper transformers soundfile mutagen jiwer pandas matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load benchmark summary data\n",
    "summary_path = Path(\"results/raw/benchmark_summary.json\")\n",
    "if not summary_path.exists():\n",
    "    summary_path = Path(\"../results/raw/benchmark_summary.json\")\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(summary_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    summary_data = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_summary = pd.DataFrame(summary_data)\n",
    "df_summary[[\"Model\", \"Clean WER\", \"Noisy WER\", \"WER Degradation\", \"Clean Latency (s)\", \"Noisy Latency (s)\", \"Clean RTF\", \"Noisy RTF\", \"CPU Memory (MB)\"]]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Benchmark Model Comparison Table\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Recognition Accuracy (WER) | Latency | Resource Usage | Ease of Deployment | Suitability for Noisy Audio |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **Faster-Whisper (`base`)** | **Clean WER:** 1.0857<br>**Noisy WER:** 1.1057<br>*(Lower is better)* | **Clean Avg:** 2.336 s (`RTF: 0.569`)<br>**Noisy Avg:** 3.502 s (`RTF: 0.842`) | **CPU Memory:** 619.7 MB<br>**GPU Peak:** 0.0 MB *(CPU mode)* | High deployment efficiency via CTranslate2 C++ engine with native INT8 CPU quantization and self-contained runtime. | Measured Clean WER: 1.0857 \| Noisy WER: 1.1057 (WER degradation = **+0.0200**). High noise robustness due to Mel-spectrogram front-end and cross-attention sequence conditioning. |\n",
    "| **OpenAI Whisper (`base`)** | **Clean WER:** 1.1018<br>**Noisy WER:** 1.1251<br>*(Lower is better)* | **Clean Avg:** 4.416 s (`RTF: 1.149`)<br>**Noisy Avg:** 4.775 s (`RTF: 1.131`) | **CPU Memory:** 840.1 MB<br>**GPU Peak:** 0.0 MB *(CPU mode)* | Standard PyTorch dependency stack requiring external FFmpeg binary on host system PATH. FP32 CPU execution with higher overhead. | Measured Clean WER: 1.1018 \| Noisy WER: 1.1251 (WER degradation = **+0.0233**). Strong noise resilience via Mel-filterbank acoustic compression and autoregressive decoding. |\n",
    "| **Wav2Vec2 (`base-960h`)** | **Clean WER:** 1.0748<br>**Noisy WER:** 1.1847<br>*(Lower is better)* | **Clean Avg:** 0.376 s (`RTF: 0.083`)<br>**Noisy Avg:** 0.368 s (`RTF: 0.081`) | **CPU Memory:** 962.9 MB<br>**GPU Peak:** 0.0 MB *(CPU mode)* | Standard Hugging Face Transformers + PyTorch stack. Acoustic-only model requiring external language model integrations for vocabulary adaptation. | Measured Clean WER: 1.0748 \| Noisy WER: 1.1847 (WER degradation = **+0.1099**). Significant noise degradation (+10.2% relative) due to unconditioned raw waveform CNN feature encoding. |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visual Comparison Charts\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10), dpi=150)\n",
    "models = df_summary[\"Model\"].tolist()\n",
    "x = np.arange(len(models))\n",
    "width = 0.35\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Clean vs Noisy WER\n",
    "axes[0, 0].bar(x - width/2, df_summary[\"Clean WER\"], width, label=\"Clean\", color=\"#3b82f6\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].bar(x + width/2, df_summary[\"Noisy WER\"], width, label=\"Noisy (10dB)\", color=\"#ef4444\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Word Error Rate (Clean vs. Noisy)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"WER (Lower is Better)\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xticks(x)\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xticklabels(models, rotation=15)\n",
    "axes[0, 0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Inference Latency\n",
    "axes[0, 1].bar(x - width/2, df_summary[\"Clean Latency (s)\"], width, label=\"Clean\", color=\"#10b981\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].bar(x + width/2, df_summary[\"Noisy Latency (s)\"], width, label=\"Noisy (10dB)\", color=\"#f59e0b\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Inference Latency per Utterance (seconds)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"Seconds (Lower is Better)\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xticks(x)\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xticklabels(models, rotation=15)\n",
    "axes[0, 1].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Real-Time Factor (RTF)\n",
    "axes[1, 0].bar(x - width/2, df_summary[\"Clean RTF\"], width, label=\"Clean RTF\", color=\"#6366f1\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].bar(x + width/2, df_summary[\"Noisy RTF\"], width, label=\"Noisy RTF\", color=\"#ec4899\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].axhline(1.0, color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\", label=\"Real-time (RTF=1.0)\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Real-Time Factor (RTF)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"RTF (<1.0 is faster than real-time)\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xticks(x)\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xticklabels(models, rotation=15)\n",
    "axes[1, 0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. CPU Memory Usage\n",
    "axes[1, 1].bar(x, df_summary[\"CPU Memory (MB)\"], width=0.5, color=\"#0284c7\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Peak CPU Resident Memory (MB)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_ylabel(\"Memory (MB)\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xticks(x)\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xticklabels(models, rotation=15)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example Single Sample Inference Demonstration\n",
    "from faster_whisper import WhisperModel\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load Faster-Whisper base model\n",
    "model = WhisperModel(\"base\", device=\"cpu\", compute_type=\"int8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Transcribe a test audio sample\n",
    "test_audio = \"data/raw/my_dataset/hi/clips/common_voice_hi_24974933.mp3\"\n",
    "start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "segments, info = model.transcribe(test_audio, task=\"transcribe\", beam_size=1)\n",
    "transcription = \" \".join([s.text for s in segments]).strip()\n",
    "elapsed = time.perf_counter() - start\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Detected Language: {info.language} ({info.language_probability:.2f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Transcription:     {transcription}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Latency:           {elapsed:.2f} seconds\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
